ecent release marked healthy in production, in all production regions. The rollback is VERIFIED and all three regions now run v2.3.0. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy in production and should not be redeployed until the failure is root-caused. Follow-up: confirm error rate recovery on v2.3.0, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure (a v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging).", "confidence": 0.9, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and the rollback is verified.\n\n- **Target version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy in production. v2.3.1 was the failing release, and v2.3.1 was running in all three regions with an error rate of 0.18.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and the follow-ups. It paged the on-call engineer.\n\nI haven't independently confirmed that the error rate has dropped since the rollback. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until its failure is root-caused. A v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}